# Jack likes Jill. Jill likes Jack. If two people like each other, they are dating.

predicate like {agent: e, patient: e}
predicate dating {agent: e, patient: e}

entity jack : e
entity jill : e

like(agent: jack, patient: jill)
like(agent: jill, patient: jack)

rule [x:e, y:e]: like(agent: x, patient: y) & like(agent: y, patient: x) -> dating(agent: x, patient: y)

? dating(agent: jack, patient: jill)